{"id": "85916", "name": "לוגריתמים – בידוד z מתוך x = e^(mz)/yⁿ (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Given</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ x=\\frac{e^{{CT:0}}}{y^{{CT:1}}}, \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>Find \\(z\\).</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(z=\\) [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Isolate \\(e^{{CT:0}}\\), then take the natural logarithm of both sides and solve for \\(z\\).</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — Isolate the exponential</b><br>Given \\(x=\\frac{e^{{CT:0}}}{y^{{CT:1}}}\\), multiply both sides by \\(y^{{CT:1}}\\):<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ e^{{CT:0}} = {{CT:2}}. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — Take the natural logarithm</b><br>The logarithm \\(\\ln\\) is the inverse of the exponential function, \\(\\ln\\left(e^{t}\\right)=t\\), so taking \\(\\ln\\) of both sides gives (both sides are positive, since \\(e^{t}>0\\)):<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}}=\\ln\\left({{CT:2}}\\right). \\]</p>Dividing by {{CT:3}}:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ z = {{CT:4}} \\]</p>By the laws of logarithms (the log of a product and the log of a power) this can also be written as \\(z={{CT:5}}\\).</div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "xy", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "answer", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "LGE-LOG-TRUE", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "LGE-LOG-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["answer", "m", "mz", "n", "xyn"], "nvariants": 16}